# Scrolling off the main thread (the APZ bargain), in four dependent parts.
# Merged from: webkit-force-async-scroll-env, webkit-independent-scroll-env,
# webkit-scrolling-thread-display-link-env, webkit-scrolling-thread-tick-env.
# Shipped default ON since build 540.
#
# None of the four does anything useful without the others, and all four are
# device-root-caused on franceinfo:
#
#  1. WEBKIT_FORCE_ASYNC_SCROLL — the page's non-composited fixed/sticky
#     elements set SynchronousScrollingReason::HasNonLayerViewportConstrained-
#     Objects, which forbids the scrolling thread from applying layer positions
#     (canUpdateLayersOnScrollingThread false): ZERO async-scroll composites,
#     every visible scroll frame waits for a full ~1 s main-thread rendering
#     update = the 1 fps notch-by-notch scroll. gdb-proven, composites:updates
#     24:23 stock vs 23:6 after neutralizing the 28 fixed/sticky elements via
#     JS. The flag drops the slow-repaint reasons at the single
#     AsyncScrollingCoordinator::setSynchronousScrollingReasons choke point.
#  2. WEBKIT_INDEPENDENT_SCROLL — upstream is a *conditional* desync: on every
#     display refresh the scrolling thread blocks on m_stateCondition for up to
#     half a frame waiting for the main thread's rendering update, and only on
#     timeout may it write scroll offsets into the compositor scene itself. So
#     every scroll frame pays a main-thread latency tax and a merely-slow main
#     thread drags scrolling with it. This makes the existing off-main-thread
#     path the default: apply layer positions + request an AsyncScrolling
#     composite on EVERY refresh, stop round-tripping willStartRenderingUpdate
#     through the scrolling thread, and stop letting sync-scrolling reasons veto
#     canUpdateLayersOnScrollingThread. Nothing in the compositor needs the main
#     thread to recomposite a committed scene.
#  3. The display-link half, which is what makes (2) actually do anything: the
#     scrolling thread's only heartbeat was owned by the main thread. The only
#     display-link observer ever registered on WPE is the main thread's
#     WebDisplayRefreshMonitor (EventDispatcher::startDisplayDidRefreshCallbacks
#     exists but is called only by MomentumEventDispatcher, not ENABLE()d for
#     WPE), DisplayRefreshMonitor drops ticks while !isPreviousFrameDone() and
#     stops the mechanism after ONE unscheduled fire, and
#     DisplayLink::notifyObserversDisplayDidRefresh skips clients with an empty
#     observer list. A stalled main thread therefore killed the display link and
#     with it the scrolling thread's tick (device-measured 59/59 sched calls;
#     scroll composites 7.3/s, scrollapply ~11/s instead of 60, 1.3 s gaps,
#     compositor ~84% idle). The vblank source was fine — it is the observer
#     bookkeeping that dies. EventDispatcher now holds its own observer while
#     the scrolling tree reports hasRecentActivity().
#  4. Its own tick, because (3) still was not enough: with 1-3 in place and a
#     verified-clean single-instance foreground rig, the scrolling thread ticked
#     ~5/s and requested AsyncScrolling composites ~3/s instead of 60, and a
#     10 s freeze contained exactly ONE scrollapply. Forcing a free-running 60 Hz
#     vblank (WEBKIT_FORCE_VBLANK_TIMER=1) made it worse (5.2/s, applies moved
#     back to the main thread), which rules out the clock source. So while a
#     scroll is live, a plain repeating timer (WEBKIT_INDEPENDENT_SCROLL_TICK_MS,
#     default 16) on the scrolling thread's own run loop drives
#     displayDidRefreshOnScrollingThread() — no display link, no IPC routing, no
#     main thread. Armed from scrollingTreeNodeDidScroll, disarms when
#     hasRecentActivity() goes false, so an idle page costs nothing and a fling
#     is self-sustaining. Sets the pace of scroll OFFSETS; the compositor still
#     throttles on frameComplete.
#
# Lossy, the same bargain as Gecko APZ: scroll-linked JS and `scroll` events fire
# at main-thread cadence, and newly-exposed content is painted only once the main
# thread runs (more low-res/checkerboard on slow pages instead of a freeze) —
# pairs with webkit-scroll-degradation. Unset/0 = stock throughout.
#
# ---
